{
  "context": "Extend benchbox.utils.printing as the canonical output API and forbid new direct Console()/print() usage\nin runtime modules. Replace command-local Console() instances with benchbox.cli.shared.console.\nFor core execution paths that can be called by CLI and MCP, route output through verbosity-aware logger\nor centralized helpers; use silence_output only as a compatibility boundary where upstream third-party\nwrites cannot be controlled directly. Add targeted tests for quiet behavior in CLI and MCP tool execution.\n",
  "description": "Audit findings show multiple user-visible output paths bypassing the centralized output mechanism:\n- direct Console() instances in CLI commands\n- raw print() in core execution/data-generation flows\n- mixed output channels in interactive shell paths\n- transitive leak risk for MCP tools that invoke core code paths\n\nThis item consolidates all user-facing output behind a central output module and enforces quiet-mode\nguarantees across CLI and MCP execution paths.",
  "legacy": {
    "anti_patterns": [
      {
        "dont": "keep command-local Console() singletons",
        "instead": "use benchbox.cli.shared.console or injected quiet-aware console",
        "item_id": "centralize-output-control-and-eliminate-print-leaks",
        "why": "they bypass shared quiet policy"
      },
      {
        "dont": "rely only on call-site silence_output wrappers",
        "instead": "route runtime output through centralized helpers/logging",
        "item_id": "centralize-output-control-and-eliminate-print-leaks",
        "why": "transitive core calls can still leak output in other entrypoints"
      },
      {
        "dont": "use bare print() in runtime execution paths",
        "instead": "use centralized printing/logging helpers",
        "item_id": "centralize-output-control-and-eliminate-print-leaks",
        "why": "it bypasses quiet controls and MCP stdout constraints"
      }
    ],
